---
import Details from '@/Details.astro'
---

<div class="flex flex-col mx-auto gap-12.5 max-w-[70ch]">
  <h3 class="text-h2 text-balance">Frequently Asked Questions</h3>
  <div class="flex flex-col">
    <Details summary="Who is this itinerary best suited to?">
      <p>
        This itinerary is best for travelers who want a considered route rather than a fast
        checklist. It works well when the traveler values pacing, atmosphere, and how one stop leads
        into the next.
      </p>
    </Details>

    <Details summary="Can this itinerary be customized?">
      <p>
        Yes. The structure provides a starting point, but the route, pace, hotel mix, and emphasis
        can be adjusted around your interests, travel style, and practical requirements.
      </p>
    </Details>

    <Details summary="Is this itinerary too busy or fairly relaxed?">
      <p>
        The answer depends on your travel rhythm. Some travelers prefer to keep momentum and see
        more range, while others benefit from fewer stops and more time in each place. The best
        itinerary usually reflects energy as much as geography.
      </p>
    </Details>

    <Details summary="Can this work for a honeymoon, family trip, or special occasion?">
      <p>
        Often yes, but the right version of the itinerary will differ by traveler. A honeymoon may
        need more privacy and pacing, while a family trip may need easier logistics and more
        flexibility.
      </p>
    </Details>

    <Details summary="Is this meant to be booked as shown?">
      <p>
        Not necessarily. Think of it as a well-shaped example of how the journey could work. Some
        travelers will want something close to this structure, while others will use it as a
        starting point for a more tailored version.
      </p>
    </Details>
  </div>
</div>
